  "notes": "Discord's developer portal (discord.com/developers/applications) lets anyone register an application and generate a bot token / OAuth2 client credentials for free, no approval gate for standard bot/API scopes (privileged intents like message content require a form but not blocking basic API access). API is REST with a large surface (guilds, channels, users, webhooks, interactions, etc., several hundred endpoints) plus a Gateway websocket for real-time events. No official vendor-published MCP server found; several community MCP servers exist (SaseQ/discord-mcp, moltis, gortex, Smithery listings).",
